## Communication Protocols

### Client ↔ Broker (WebSocket/Socket.IO)

Standard Socket.IO connection:

```
wss://broker.example.com/
```

Events are validated with Zod schemas defined in `packages/realtime/src/events/`.

### Server → Broker (TCP with HMAC)

Custom binary protocol for serverless compatibility (no persistent connections):

```
Frame Format:
┌─────────────┬─────────────────┬──────────────┐
│ Length (4B) │ JSON Payload    │ HMAC-SHA256  │
│  uint32 BE  │ (variable)      │   (32B)      │
└─────────────┴─────────────────┴──────────────┘
```

The HMAC signature ensures only services with `REALTIME_SECRET_KEY` can emit events.

## Event Types

### Client Events (`client-events.ts`)

Events the browser sends to the broker:

```ts
"room:join"      → { roomId: string }
"room:leave"     → { roomId: string }
"message:send"   → { roomId: string, content: string }
"cursor:move"    → { roomId: string, x: number, y: number }
"doc:join"       → { documentId: string }
"doc:update"     → { documentId: string, update: string }
```

### Server Events (`server-events.ts`)

Events the backend sends to the broker via TCP:

```ts
"notification:send" → { userId: string, title: string, message: string }
"room:broadcast"    → { roomId: string, event: string, data: unknown }
```

### Broker Events (`broker-events.ts`)

Events the broker sends to clients:

```ts
"connection:info"   → { user: { id, name } }
"notification:new"  → { title: string, message: string }
"message:new"       → { roomId, user, content, timestamp }
"cursor:update"     → { roomId, user, x, y }
"room:sync"         → { roomId, users: [...] }
"doc:sync"          → { documentId, state }
"doc:update"        → { documentId, update }
```

## Database Integration (Broker)

The broker can connect directly to PostgreSQL for features like Yjs document persistence:

```
apps/realtime/
├── src/lib/
│   └── documents/
│       ├── database.ts   # Drizzle connection
│       ├── state.ts      # In-memory Y.Doc management
│       └── operations.ts # Load/save with debounce
```

Documents are saved with debouncing (3s) to avoid excessive writes during collaborative editing.

## Security Summary

| Channel | Protection |
|---------|-----------|
| Client ↔ Broker | WSS (TLS) |
| Server → Broker | TCP + HMAC-SHA256 signature |

## Environment Variables

### Broker (`apps/realtime`)

```
REALTIME_SECRET_KEY  # Shared secret (32+ chars)
WS_PORT              # WebSocket port (default: 3001)
TCP_PORT             # Internal TCP port (default: 9000)
ALLOWED_ORIGINS      # CORS origins (comma-separated)
API_URL              # Web app URL for Better Auth session verification
```

### Web App (`apps/web`)

```
REALTIME_SECRET_KEY       # Same shared secret
REALTIME_TCP_URL          # tcp://broker:9000
```

## Preview Environments

For PR preview deployments, see `.cursor/rules/project/preview-environments.mdc`.

The system automatically links Vercel preview deployments with Railway PR environments:
- GitHub Actions detects Vercel deployment success
- Updates Railway `API_URL` to point to Vercel preview
- Railway realtime service authenticates against the correct preview
